  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.header": "How to build a gregtech multiblock",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_1": "First, you need a assembly line main block.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_10": "Place the storage part of the AE subnet.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_11": "Please note that quartz fiber should be used to disconnect the direct connection between the subnet and the main network, while also supplying power to the subnet.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_12": "Set the priority of the storage bus, decreasing from the main block direction to the output bus, which means whether your materials will enter the assembly line in the correct order for synthesis.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_13": "Connecting to the power grid.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_14": "Place the \u0027one click template\u0027 (\u0027+\u0027button) in the template encoding terminal of the pattern provide to ensure that the materials are output to the buffer in the correct order.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_15": "Change the lock synthesis mode to \u0027until the main product is returned\u0027 on the left side of the pattern provide.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_16": "Put in the research data required for the formula",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_17": "Congratulations, you have learned how to use AE2 for assembly line automation.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_2": "One click placement using the terminal.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_3": "ulv output bus",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_4": "quadruple input hatch",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_5": "ulv input bus",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_6": "Place the pattern provider in the AE main network, paying attention to place to closely to the ULV output bus.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_7": "Use a wrench to adjust the sample supplier to send material upwards.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_8": "Place any level of buffer, pay attention to place to closely following the quadruple input hatch.",
  "kubejs.ponder.assembly_line_building.text_9": "Set automatic output direction for items",
  "kubejs.ponder.blaze.header": "How to spawn blaze without entering nether",
  "kubejs.ponder.blaze.text_1": "Under normal circumstances, we cannot encounter the blaze before entering nether.",
  "kubejs.ponder.blaze.text_2": "Under normal circumstances, this is the way snow golem are placed.",
  "kubejs.ponder.blaze.text_3": "Now all you need to do is replace the snow blocks with iron bars, carved pumpkin with fel pumpkin, and you can spawn a blaze to use.",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.header": "kinetic input/output hatch",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_1": "This is kinetic hatch,they have different levels.",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_2": "The lowest level of kinetic hatch you may use is the LV kinetic hatch,it have 32768su input/output at 256RPM speed.",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_3": "Similar to gregtech\u0027s boost mechanism,the required stress * 4 is required for each level of the kinetic hatch",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_4": "131072su",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_5": "524288su",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_6": "2097152su",
  "kubejs.ponder.block_ponder.text_7": "8388608su",
